 "c_sql": {
  "cat": "code",
  "prompt": "Write a SQL query selecting the name and salary of the top 3 highest-paid employees from a table 'employees(name, salary)'.",
  "answer": "# SQL Query: Top 3 Highest-Paid Employees\n\n```sql\nSELECT name, salary\nFROM employees\nORDER BY salary DESC\nLIMIT 3;\n```\n\n## Explanation\n\n| Clause | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `SELECT name, salary` | Retrieves only the two columns we need |\n| `FROM employees` | Specifies the source table |\n| `ORDER BY salary DESC` | Sorts employees from highest to lowest salary |\n| `LIMIT 3` | Restricts the result to the first 3 rows |\n\n## Handling Ties (Optional)\n\nIf you want to include **all employees tied** at the 3rd-highest salary, use `DENSE_RANK()`:\n\n```sql\nSELECT name, salary\nFROM (\n    SELECT name, salary,\n           DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS rnk\n    FROM employees\n) ranked\nWHERE rnk <= 3;\n```\n\n## Database-Specific Syntax\n\n- **MySQL / PostgreSQL / SQLite:** `LIMIT 3` \u2705\n- **SQL Server / Oracle:** use `TOP` or `FETCH FIRST`:\n\n```sql\n-- SQL Server\nSELECT TOP 3 name, salary\nFROM employees\nORDER BY salary DESC;\n\n-- Oracle 12c+\nSELECT name, salary\nFROM employees\nORDER BY salary DESC\nFETCH FIRST 3 ROWS ONLY;\n```",
